  "query_preview": "/Thursday through Monday/...\nIssued 359 AM MDT MON OCT 5 2026\nThe ridge will remain overhead through Friday, keeping\ntemperatures 10 to 20 degrees above normal under mostly clear\nskies. Winds will start to pick up on Friday across the higher \nterrain as an upper level trough approaches from the north. The \ntrough will push a cold front through the area on Saturday, \nbringing cooler temperatures and breezy conditions. Highs are \nforecast to cool by 10 to 15 degrees from Friday, but ensemble \nvariability in the timing of the front reduces confidence in the\ntemperature forecast for Saturday. The trough is favored to \ndeepen over the Pacific Northwest, and may move overhead as a \nclosed low. This will continue the cooling trend on Sunday and \nMonday, with highs decreasing another 10 to 15 degrees. \nA chance of precipitation will develop especially east of the \nlow with a 20-40% chance of rain and high mountain snow across \ncentral/south central Idaho, and a 10-20% chance further west. \nWinds will remain breezy under this pattern.",
